\f0\fs24 \cf0 SWING TRADING SIGNAL GENERATOR \'97 SPEC DOCUMENT\
===============================================\
\
PURPOSE\
-------\
Build a tool that collects 5 to 6 years of daily price data for 100 financial\
instruments from Yahoo Finance, calculates an 18-period moving average ribbon,\
identifies buying and selling signals, and tracks key price levels. Output goes\
to Google Sheets, run daily via terminal (cron scheduler).\
\
\
INSTRUMENTS\
-----------\
100 financial instruments. List provided separately in a text file.\
\
\
DATA SOURCE & HISTORY\
---------------------\
Provider:   Yahoo Finance\
Daily data: 5 to 6 years minimum\
Collect all available fields from Yahoo Finance, not just the minimum.\
\
\
MOVING AVERAGE RIBBON\
---------------------\
18 simple moving averages (SMA) calculated on the daily timeframe.\
Start: 38 | Increment: +7 | End: 150\
\
Values: 38, 45, 52, 59, 66, 73, 80, 87, 94, 101, 108, 115, 122, 129, 136, 143, 150\
\
Note: Confirm final count equals 18 during build.\
\
This ribbon defines trend direction for every instrument.\
\
\
TREND DEFINITION\
----------------\
UPTREND:   Price closes ABOVE all 18 moving averages.\
DOWNTREND: Price closes BELOW all 18 moving averages.\
NEUTRAL:   Price is between the moving averages \'97 no confirmed trend.\
\
\
PRIMARY SIGNALS (strongest \'97 flag prominently)\
-----------------------------------------------\
P1 \'97 TREND CHANGE\
  Price crosses the entire ribbon and closes on the opposite side.\
  Buy:  Was below all MAs, crosses full ribbon, closes above the 38 MA.\
  Sell: Was above all MAs, crosses full ribbon, closes below the 150 MA.\
\
P2 \'97 150 MA BOUNCE\
  In an established trend, price pulls back to the 150 MA, touches or briefly\
  pierces it, then reverses sharply without closing on the other side.\
  Buy:  Uptrend. Pullback reaches 150 MA, sharp reversal, closes back above.\
  Sell: Downtrend. Rally reaches 150 MA, sharp reversal, closes back below.\
\
P3 \'97 SMALL MA REVERSAL (UPTREND)\
  In an uptrend, price pulls back to the smaller MAs (38\'9680 range) and gives\
  a sharp single or double bottom, then reverses upward.\
  Buy:  Close above the touched MA after reversal.\
  Sell: Not applicable.\
\
P4 \'97 SMALL MA REVERSAL (DOWNTREND)\
  In a downtrend, price rallies to the smaller MAs (38\'9680 range) and gives\
  a sharp top, then reverses downward.\
  Buy:  Not applicable.\
  Sell: Close below the touched MA after reversal.\
\
\
SECONDARY SIGNALS (valid entry points, more frequent)\
------------------------------------------------------\
Buy:  Uptrend confirmed. Price pulls back and touches ANY MA in the ribbon,\
      then reverses upward.\
Sell: Downtrend confirmed. Price rallies and touches ANY MA in the ribbon,\
      then reverses downward.\
\
\
WATCH LIST (approaching but not touched \'97 do NOT trade yet)\
-----------------------------------------------------------\
Buy setup:  Uptrend. Price declining toward MAs for 1\'962 days.\
            Flag as: "Watch \'97 approaching MA, potential buy setup"\
Sell setup: Downtrend. Price rallying toward MAs for 1\'962 days.\
            Flag as: "Watch \'97 approaching MA, potential sell setup"\
\
\
POTENTIAL TURNING POINT (structural alert \'97 not a trade signal)\
---------------------------------------------------------------\
Trigger: Trend has run for 200+ trading days (approx. 3 quarters or more).\
         Price pulls back halfway into the ribbon and bounces from the midpoint\
         rather than reaching the extreme MAs.\
Flag as: "Potential turning point \'97 trend 200+ days, midpoint bounce detected.\
          May take weeks or months to develop."\
Applies in both uptrends and downtrends.\
\
\
SIGNAL CONFIRMATION STATES (one status per instrument per day)\
--------------------------------------------------------------\
  Uptrend \'97 no signal\
  Uptrend \'97 watch, approaching MA\
  Uptrend \'97 waiting for reversal confirmation\
  Uptrend \'97 secondary buy signal confirmed\
  Uptrend \'97 primary buy signal confirmed [P1 / P2 / P3 / P4]\
  Downtrend \'97 no signal\
  Downtrend \'97 watch, approaching MA\
  Downtrend \'97 waiting for reversal confirmation\
  Downtrend \'97 secondary sell signal confirmed\
  Downtrend \'97 primary sell signal confirmed [P1 / P2 / P3 / P4]\
  Neutral \'97 no confirmed trend direction\
  Potential turning point detected\
\
\
VOLUME ANALYSIS\
---------------\
Collect daily volume for every instrument.\
Calculate average volume over a 20\'9630 day lookback period.\
If today's volume exceeds that average: flag column as "volume spike".\
Column name: volume_spike_flag\
\
\
KEY PRICE LEVELS \'97 HISTORICAL TOPS AND BOTTOMS\
-----------------------------------------------\
The code must identify significant historical top and bottom price levels\
from the full 5 to 6 year dataset for each instrument.\
\
A top level is a price high that acted as resistance \'97 where price reached\
a peak and then reversed downward.\
A bottom level is a price low that acted as support \'97 where price reached\
a trough and then reversed upward.\
\
For each instrument, track the following per level:\
\
  key_level_price       \'97 the price of the historical top or bottom\
  key_level_type        \'97 "top" or "bottom"\
  key_level_date        \'97 the date that level was first established\
  key_level_touch_count \'97 how many times price has reached or touched\
                          that level across the full history\
  key_level_touched_today \'97 yes or no: did today's price action reach\
                            or touch this level\
\
When today's price touches or reaches a historical top or bottom level,\
flag it clearly in the output. These are significant areas where price\
has previously reversed and may do so again.\
\
\
EXCEL / GOOGLE SHEETS OUTPUT\
-----------------------------\
Structure:     One sheet per trading day\
Rows:          100 (one per instrument)\
Destination:   Google Sheets on Google Drive\
Automation:    Run daily via terminal cron scheduler\
\
COLUMN ORDER PER ROW:\
\
  instrument_name\
  date\
  open\
  high\
  low\
  close\
  volume\
  volume_average (20\'9630 day)\
  volume_spike_flag\
  ma_38, ma_45, ma_52, ma_59, ma_66, ma_73, ma_80, ma_87, ma_94,\
  ma_101, ma_108, ma_115, ma_122, ma_129, ma_136, ma_143, ma_150\
  trend_direction\
  confirmation_status\
  primary_signal\
  secondary_signal\
  watch_flag\
  potential_turning_point_flag\
  key_level_price\
  key_level_type\
  key_level_date\
  key_level_touch_count\
  key_level_touched_today\
  [all additional fields available from Yahoo Finance]\
\
\
TRADING RULES\
-------------\
Valid entries:    Primary signals and secondary signals only.\
No-trade zone:    Watch list stage \'97 wait for a confirmed signal before entering.\
Goal:             Identify only the safest buying and selling points.\
\
\
PERFORMANCE NOTES\
-----------------\
- Daily timeframe only \'97 no weekly or monthly data.\
- Collect all available Yahoo Finance fields \'97 more data is better.\
- The code will be run from terminal on a daily schedule using cron.\
\
\
PHASE 2 (future)\
----------------\
Once the data tool is working, a separate app will be built to visualize\
and interact with the signals. A separate requirements document will cover\
that phase.\
\
